If you're learning this for your ML journey, focus in this order:

1. Understand what a time series is
2. Learn trend and seasonality
3. Learn datetime handling with Pandas
4. Learn lag features
5. Learn rolling statistics
6. Understand train/test splitting without shuffling
7. Learn autocorrelation, ACF and PACF
8. Understand stationarity and differencing
9. Learn forecasting baselines
10. Learn ARIMA/SARIMA
11. Learn ML-based forecasting
12. Learn proper time-series evaluation and avoid leakage

The most important idea to carry forward is this:

Time-series data is different from ordinary tabular data because the order of observations contains information. When building a model, you must respect that order and make sure the model never gets information from the future that wouldn't have been available at prediction time.
